_model: proposition
---
title: Proposition 16
---
order: 16
---
short_label: VI.16
---
sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: If four straight lines are proportional, then the rectangle contained by the extremes equals the rectangle contained by the means; and, if the rectangle contained by the extremes equals the rectangle contained by the means, then the four straight lines are proportional.
----
proof:

Let the four straight lines {AB}, {CD}, {E}, and {F} be proportional, so that {AB} is to {CD} as {E} is to {F}.

I say that the rectangle {AB} by {F} equals the rectangle {CD} by {E}.

Draw {AG} and {CH} from the points {A} and {C} at right angles to the straight lines {AB} and {CD}, and make {AG} equal to {F}, and {CH} equal to {E}. [!just I.11; I.3]

Complete the parallelograms {BG|BGt} and {DH|DHt}. [!just I.31]

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="380" height="220" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="VI.16 diagram" src="propVI16.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
    // Euclid erects AG, CH at right angles to AB, CD, equal to F and E
    // (I.11, I.3), completes the rectangles BG, DH (I.31), and reads both
    // directions off VI.14 with V.7.
    //
    // Joyce's figure draws the two filled parallelograms and the lines E, F;
    // AB, AG, CD, CH are only parallelogram sides there. The walk needs them
    // before the parallelograms exist, so ABs, CDs, AGs, CHs are solid slide
    // twins over those sides, hidden at rest (initiallyHidden); AGs and CHs
    // are declared A→G and C→H so they stroke from A and C as drawn. The
    // names AB, CD, AG, CH are transparent targets for captions and prose. The right
    // angles at A and C ("at right angles", by construction) are red
    // angleMarkerRight squares, hidden at rest. Highlighting a filled
    // parallelogram would raise its face over them (#140), so caption and
    // prose refs to BG and DH go to the faceless twins BGt / DHt.
    //
    // The statement slides stand over the resting figure, since they speak
    // of the rectangles; the proof then withdraws to the givens, and the
    // converse ("With the same construction") rebuilds it.
    //
    // Draggables (checked against the bundle): A, B, C, D free, the guide
    // ends L0, L1 (invisible) and the lineSliders E0, E1, F0, F1 that fix E
    // and F — all givens on slide 1. G and H are derived (cutoff) and listed
    // per slide; nothing to defer.
    var GIVEN = ["A","B","C","D","AB","CD","ABs","CDs","E","F"];
    var PERP  = GIVEN.concat(["AG","CH","AGs","CHs","rtA","rtC"]);
    var CUT   = PERP.concat(["G","H"]);
    var ALL   = CUT.concat(["BG","DH","BGt","DHt"]);
    geomlib.init({
        canvasid: "canvas_0",
        background: "35,19,100",
        title: "VI.16",
        elements: [
            "A;point;free;40,120",
            "B;point;free;170,120",
            "C;point;free;220,150",
            "D;point;free;350,150",
            "L0;point;free;-1000,190;0;0",
            "L1;point;free;1000,190;0;0",
            "E0;point;lineSlider;L0,L1,40,0;0",
            "E1;point;lineSlider;L0,L1,140,0;0",
            "E;line;connect;E0,E1;black",
            "F0;point;lineSlider;L0,L1,220,0;0",
            "F1;point;lineSlider;L0,L1,290,0;0",
            "F;line;connect;F0,F1;black",
            "G';point;perpendicular;A,B;0;0",
            "G;point;cutoff;A,G',F0,F1",
            "BG;polygon;parallelogram;B,A,G;0;0;black;random",
            "H';point;perpendicular;C,D;0;0",
            "H;point;cutoff;C,H',E0,E1",
            "DH;polygon;parallelogram;D,C,H;0;0;black;random",
            // Slide twins over the parallelogram sides (see above).
            "ABs;line;connect;A,B",
            "CDs;line;connect;C,D",
            "AGs;line;connect;A,G",
            "CHs;line;connect;C,H",
            // The same four as transparent highlight targets, standing at
            // rest so the prose hovers light them.
            "AB;line;connect;A,B;0;0;0",
            "CD;line;connect;C,D;0;0;0",
            "AG;line;connect;A,G;0;0;0",
            "CH;line;connect;C,H;0;0;0",
            // The parallelograms as highlight targets. Faceless.
            "BGt;polygon;parallelogram;B,A,G;0;0;0;0",
            "DHt;polygon;parallelogram;D,C,H;0;0;0;0",
            "rtA;sector;angleMarkerRight;A,B,G;0;0;red;red",
            "rtC;sector;angleMarkerRight;C,D,H;0;0;red;red"
        ],
        initiallyHidden: ["ABs","CDs","AGs","CHs"],
        slides: [
            { text: "“If four straight lines are proportional,”",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AB","CD","E","F"] },
            { text: "“then the rectangle contained by the extremes equals the rectangle contained by the means;”",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["BGt","DHt"] },
            { text: "“and, if the rectangle contained by the extremes equals the rectangle contained by the means,”",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["BGt","DHt"] },
            { text: "“then the four straight lines are proportional.”",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AB","CD","E","F"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "VI.16" }] },
            { text: "Let the four straight lines {AB}, {CD}, {E}, and {F} be proportional,",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["AB","CD","E","F"] },
            { text: "so that {AB} is to {CD} as {E} is to {F}.",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["AB","CD","E","F"] },
            { text: "I say that the rectangle {AB} by {F} equals the rectangle {CD} by {E}.",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["AB","F","CD","E"] },
            { text: "Draw {AG} and {CH} from the points {A} and {C} at right angles to the straight lines {AB} and {CD},",
              visible: PERP,
              highlighted: ["AG","CH","rtA","rtC"],
              transition: { mode: "cascade", animations: [
                  { elem: "AGs", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "rtA", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep },
                  { elem: "CHs", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "rtC", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] },
              justifications: [{ claim: "AG, CH at right angles to AB, CD", ref: "I.11" }] },
            { text: "and make {AG} equal to {F}, and {CH} equal to {E}.",
              visible: CUT,
              highlighted: ["AG","F","CH","E","G","H"],
              transition: { mode: "parallel", animations: [
                  { elem: "G", name: geomlib.A.Point.appear },
                  { elem: "H", name: geomlib.A.Point.appear } ] },
              justifications: [{ claim: "AG cut off equal to F, CH to E", ref: "I.3" }] },
            { text: "Complete the parallelograms {BG|BGt} and {DH|DHt}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["BGt","DHt"],
              transition: { mode: "parallel", animations: [
                  { elem: "BG", name: geomlib.A.Polygon.outlineAndFill },
                  { elem: "DH", name: geomlib.A.Polygon.outlineAndFill } ] },
              justifications: [{ ref: "I.31" }] },
            { text: "Then since {AB} is to {CD} as {E} is to {F}, while {E} equals {CH}, and {F} equals {AG},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AB","CD","E","F","CH","AG"] },
            { text: "therefore {AB} is to {CD} as {CH} is to {AG}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AB","CD","CH","AG"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "equals have the same ratio", ref: "V.7" }] },
            { text: "Therefore in the parallelograms {BG|BGt} and {DH|DHt} the sides about the equal angles are reciprocally proportional.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["BGt","DHt","rtA","rtC","AB","CD","CH","AG"] },
            { text: "But those equiangular parallelograms in which the sides about the equal angles are reciprocally proportional are equal,",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["BGt","DHt","rtA","rtC"] },
            { text: "therefore the parallelogram {BG|BGt} equals the parallelogram {DH|DHt}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["BGt","DHt"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "equiangular, sides reciprocally proportional: equal", ref: "VI.14" }] },
            { text: "And {BG|BGt} is the rectangle {AB} by {F}, for {AG} equals {F},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["BGt","AB","F","AG"] },
            { text: "and {DH|DHt} is the rectangle {CD} by {E}, for {E} equals {CH},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["DHt","CD","E","CH"] },
            { text: "therefore the rectangle {AB} by {F} equals the rectangle {CD} by {E}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AB","F","CD","E","BGt","DHt"] },
            { text: "Next, let the rectangle {AB} by {F} be equal to the rectangle {CD} by {E}.",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["AB","F","CD","E"] },
            { text: "I say that the four straight lines are proportional, so that {AB} is to {CD} as {E} is to {F}.",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["AB","CD","E","F"] },
            { text: "With the same construction, since the rectangle {AB} by {F} equals the rectangle {CD} by {E},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AB","F","CD","E"],
              transition: { mode: "cascade", animations: [
                  { elem: "AGs", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "CHs", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "BG", name: geomlib.A.Polygon.outlineAndFill },
                  { elem: "DH", name: geomlib.A.Polygon.outlineAndFill } ] } },
            { text: "and the rectangle {AB} by {F} is {BG|BGt}, for {AG} equals {F},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AB","F","BGt","AG"] },
            { text: "and the rectangle {CD} by {E} is {DH|DHt}, for {CH} equals {E},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["CD","E","DHt","CH"] },
            { text: "therefore {BG|BGt} equals {DH|DHt}. And they are equiangular.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["BGt","DHt","rtA","rtC"] },
            { text: "But in equal and equiangular parallelograms the sides about the equal angles are reciprocally proportional.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["BGt","DHt","AB","CD","CH","AG"] },
            { text: "Therefore {AB} is to {CD} as {CH} is to {AG}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AB","CD","CH","AG"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "equal and equiangular: sides reciprocally proportional", ref: "VI.14" }] },
            { text: "But {CH} equals {E}, and {AG} equals {F},",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["CH","E","AG","F"] },
            { text: "therefore {AB} is to {CD} as {E} is to {F}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AB","CD","E","F"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "equals have the same ratio", ref: "V.7" }] },
            { text: "Therefore, if four straight lines are proportional,",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AB","CD","E","F"] },
            { text: "then the rectangle contained by the extremes equals the rectangle contained by the means;",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["BGt","DHt"] },
            { text: "and, if the rectangle contained by the extremes equals the rectangle contained by the means,",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["BGt","DHt"] },
            { text: "then the four straight lines are proportional.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["AB","CD","E","F"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "Q.E.D." }] }
        ],
        resolveJustification: function(ref) {
            if (ref === "VI.16") return "#prop";
            return (window.eucrefs && window.eucrefs[ref]) || null;
        }
    });

    // Per-page citation lookup for the slideshow's resolveJustification.
    window.eucrefs = (window.eucrefs || {});
    Object.assign(window.eucrefs, {
        "I.3":   "/elements/books/bookI/propositions/propI3/",
        "I.11":  "/elements/books/bookI/propositions/propI11/",
        "I.31":  "/elements/books/bookI/propositions/propI31/",
        "V.7":   "/elements/books/bookV/propositions/propV7/",
        "VI.14": "/elements/books/bookVI/propositions/propVI14/"
    });
</script>
</figure>

Then since {AB} is to {CD} as {E} is to {F}, while {E} equals {CH}, and {F} equals {AG}, therefore {AB} is to {CD} as {CH} is to {AG}. [!just V.7]

Therefore in the parallelograms {BG|BGt} and {DH|DHt} the sides about the equal angles are reciprocally proportional.

But those equiangular parallelograms in which the sides about the equal angles are reciprocally proportional are equal, therefore the parallelogram {BG|BGt} equals the parallelogram {DH|DHt}. [!just VI.14]

And {BG|BGt} is the rectangle {AB} by {F}, for {AG} equals {F}, and {DH|DHt} is the rectangle {CD} by {E}, for {E} equals {CH}, therefore the rectangle {AB} by {F} equals the rectangle {CD} by {E}.

<hr width="50%">

Next, let the rectangle {AB} by {F} be equal to the rectangle {CD} by {E}.

I say that the four straight lines are proportional, so that {AB} is to {CD} as {E} is to {F}.

With the same construction, since the rectangle {AB} by {F} equals the rectangle {CD} by {E}, and the rectangle {AB} by {F} is {BG|BGt}, for {AG} equals {F}, and the rectangle {CD} by {E} is {DH|DHt}, for {CH} equals {E}, therefore {BG|BGt} equals {DH|DHt}. And they are equiangular.

But in equal and equiangular parallelograms the sides about the equal angles are reciprocally proportional. Therefore {AB} is to {CD} as {CH} is to {AG}. [!just VI.14]

But {CH} equals {E}, and {AG} equals {F}, therefore {AB} is to {CD} as {E} is to {F}. [!just V.7]

Therefore, *if four straight lines are proportional, then the rectangle contained by the extremes equals the rectangle contained by the means; and, if the rectangle contained by the extremes equals the rectangle contained by the means, then the four straight lines are proportional.*

<div class="qed">Q.E.D.</div>
----
guide: This proposition is a special case of @VI.14. It hardly needs such a protracted proof. It is used occasionally in Book X, but the special case when the means are equal and the second figure is a square, as enunciated in the next proposition, is used throughout Book X and frequently in Book XIII.
